{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1470196-trinity-continuum-aeon-group-theory","id":1470196,"title":"[Trinity Continuum] Aeon Group Theory","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-11T01:17:27-08:00","id":1470196,"title":"[Trinity Continuum] Aeon Group Theory","content":"I'm preparing multi-era <b>Continuum</b> game - so I analyze setting major elements between eras. One of corner stones of <b>Continuum</b> is <i><b>Aeon</b></i> organization, across all of them.<br /> <br /> So let's start with basic recap - point me where I'm wrong or things are unclear. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b><i>\u00c6on</i> was founded in Chicago in June 1923</b> by Maxwell Anderson Mercer, Michael Damien Donighal, and Whitley Styles - almost a year after Hammersmith Incident that returned Quantum Energies to Earth. ( Then known as Telluric Energies. ) Mentioned previous three and few other people starte the <i><b>\u00c6on Society for Gentlemen</b></i> - formed to pursue the strange and seek out answers to the question, \u201cWhy?\u201d Its members strive to explain the inexplicable and explore uncharted territories, all in the name of doing good and sharing the knowledge they gain from their adventures with the world. While Max and Whitley remain with the organization, Michael has restyled himself <i>Doctor Primoris</i>, and has stepped away, though he does lend his aid to them<br /> from time to time in that time. ( See <b>TC Adventure!</b> )<br /> <br /> Though the <b><i>\u00c6on</i> Society</b> was originally a \u201cGentleman\u2019s Club\u201d - that part of its name was dropped before the decade was out ( Circa 1930 ). Mercer had seen the future \u2014 not only of his own organization, but of the very world \u2014 and wanted the group to be welcoming to any and all who shared the <b>Society</b>\u2019s values.<br /> <br /> In coming decades, <b><i>\u00c6on </i></b>became part Non-Profit <b><i>\u00c6on</i> Foundation</b> with distinct corporate culture ( Directors, top-down hierarchy ) - part secret society. Previous 'Society' of 1920s and 30s became 'Inner Society' that governed group on fundamental ideals, even if front was much more hierarchical as typical corporate-like group. In 2060s and 2070s Group renamed itself to <b><i>\u00c6on Covenant,</i></b> as 'covenant with humanity on it's core missions'. ( see <b>TC Core</b> and <b>TC Anima</b> )<br /> <br /> Sometimes in 2100s <b><i>\u00c6on Covenant </i></b>became <b><i>\u00c6on</i> Trinity </b>- base on it's then three main projects/subgroups: <i>Neptune</i>, <i>Triton</i>, and <i>Proteus</i>. <b><i>\u00c6on </i></b>closely cooperates with general United Nation then.<br /> <br /> <b>Am I getting it right?</b><br /> <br /> Bonus question - In <b>TC Aeon</b> era, <b>United Nations headquarters are in New York in fascists FSA - or on cosmopolitan Luna?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-20-2022, 03:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T02:40:15-08:00","id":1470199,"title":"","content":"The Aeon Society was never specifically &quot;For Gentlemen&quot; even in its inception. At least in the first edition one of the founding members was a woman and women were always welcomed to join. The &quot;For Gentlemen&quot; was mostly just there because such clubs were normally, well, for gentlemen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T05:00:37-08:00","id":1470213,"title":"","content":"The Hammersmith incident didn\u2019t \u201creturned Quantum to Earth\u201d, it was supposed to be a infinite energy engine, working on Telluric energy. It worked in a \u201cunconventional way\u201d and delivered a huge amount of energy very fast, exploding.<br /> <br /> Telluric Energy is not Quantum, well, not only Quantum, it is a set of energies that they could not figure out and differentiate, but had similar results in the results, imagine you have a black and white camera and you want to differentiate blue light from red light from green light, they could not diferentiate the 3 and called it Telluric Energy. In practice, it is a mix of Quantum, Psi and Flux, but their tech could not see the difference, to be honest \u00c6on start differentiating the 3 effectively sometime between Adventure and N-Day and effectively measure it as different things just after Aberrant era.<br /> <br /> Doc Primoris was effective member and funder of \u00c6on Society until some time during/after WWII.<br /> <br /> \u00c6on Society was in touch with UN since before N-Day, but got really powerful after it, with one of their projects, Utopia, becoming important with Novas. \u00c6on even got a chair in one of the main Councils, if I am not wrong, what put it above many countries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T07:31:11-08:00","id":1470220,"title":"","content":"Utopia got an advisory chair on the Security Council, but since Utopia was effectively controlled by Aeon you\u2019re not wrong either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T08:01:56-08:00","id":1470222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1470196-trinity-continuum-aeon-group-theory#post1470196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm preparing multi-era <b>Continuum</b> game - so I analyze setting major elements between eras. One of corner stones of <b>Continuum</b> is <i><b>Aeon</b></i> organization, across all of them.<br /> <br /> So let's start with basic recap - point me where I'm wrong or things are unclear. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b><i>\u00c6on</i> was founded in Chicago in June 1923</b> by Maxwell Anderson Mercer, Michael Damien Donighal, and Whitley Styles</div> </div> </div> </div>The full roster of founding members were Max Mercer, Michael Donighal, Whitley Styles, Annabelle Lee Newfield, Jake Stefokowski, Jack Tallon, and Benjamin Franklin Dixon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> almost a year after Hammersmith Incident that returned Quantum Energies to Earth. ( Then known as Telluric Energies. ) </div> </div> </div>&quot;Telluric Energy&quot; wasn't strictly Quantum. It's a mishmash of all three esoteric energies: quantum, psi, and flux.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In coming decades, <b><i>\u00c6on </i></b>became part Non-Profit <b><i>\u00c6on</i> Foundation</b> with distinct corporate culture ( Directors, top-down hierarchy ) - part secret society. </div> </div> </div>There's a single reference to an &quot;\u00c6on Foundation&quot;. Up to you if you want to use it as canon or not. At the moment, I consider it to be an error that slipped past us, which it was.<br /> <br /> \u00c6on Society for Gentlemen (1923) -&gt; \u00c6on Society ~(1930) -&gt; \u00c6on Covenant (~2070) -&gt; \u00c6on Trinity (~2100)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bonus question - In <b>TC Aeon</b> era, <b>United Nations headquarters are in New York in fascists FSA - or on cosmopolitan Luna?</b> </div> </div> </div>The UN is headquartered on Luna, as shown on the illustration on \u00c6on page 42, and mentioned on page 65.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Planguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1470196-trinity-continuum-aeon-group-theory?p=1470199#post1470199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Aeon Society was never specifically &quot;For Gentlemen&quot; even in its inception. At least in the first edition one of the founding members was a woman and women were always welcomed to join. The &quot;For Gentlemen&quot; was mostly just there because such clubs were normally, well, for gentlemen.</div> </div> </div> </div>To clarify this statement: the \u00c6on Society definitely had &quot;for Gentlemen&quot; as part of the organization's name, but it was never limited to men, and they dropped that part of the name by the '30s. Max's definition of &quot;Gentlemen&quot; was inclusive, not limited to gender (or even to humans), but eventually recognized that not everyone would interpret it the same way he did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T10:01:40-08:00","id":1470226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1470196-trinity-continuum-aeon-group-theory?p=1470222#post1470222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To clarify this statement: the \u00c6on Society definitely had &quot;for Gentlemen&quot; as part of the organization's name, but it was never limited to men, and they dropped that part of the name by the '30s. Max's definition of &quot;Gentlemen&quot; was inclusive, not limited to gender (<b>or even to humans</b>), but eventually recognized that not everyone would interpret it the same way he did.</div> </div> </div> </div>Felicia Smith as part of Aeon confirmed!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T11:37:44-08:00","id":1470228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1470196-trinity-continuum-aeon-group-theory?p=1470226#post1470226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Felicia Smith as part of Aeon confirmed!</div> </div> </div> </div>Part yes, funding member no. The only woman amount the funders was Crackshot, and she was a girl at the time (16 yo if I am not wrong). It was not well received by Jack \u201cSafari\u201d Tallon, until she proved her usefulness to the team and got his respect (he was a Victorian era explorer, sexist and racist, but eventually got rid of this prejudices, at least in 1e).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T13:55:54-08:00","id":1470239,"title":"","content":"Mateus? I am aware. It was just a joke. Not a statement of fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T14:22:28-08:00","id":1470241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1470196-trinity-continuum-aeon-group-theory?p=1470226#post1470226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Felicia Smith as part of Aeon confirmed!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking of Enkidu in particular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}